    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "I am going to save you some time and close this PR as it's clearly not ready. Please don't push LLM output straight to a PR, that is way too noisy and wastes maintainer time.\r\n\r\nIterate on your own fork (if you need to run CI in addition to local tests, open a PR against your fork's `master`). Once you are happy with the results, **manually** clean up the commits (squash as much as possible, add **concise** descriptive commit messages, create a similar PR description) and only _then_ open a PR against upstream.\r\n\r\nFor more involved changes that are not purely self-contained, it is also better to discuss the approach _first_, e.g., in comments to the original issue. You can also open a Discussion and ping a relevant maintainer with questions.",
            "created_at": "2026-07-31T17:34:41Z",
